<title>FRANCE: Lagardere says confident on Thomson-CSF.</title>
<headline>Lagardere says confident on Thomson-CSF.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Missiles-to-publishing group Lagardere said on Wednesday it was &quot;serene and confident&quot; on Thomson-CSF, which the government said earlier it planned to sell through a private placement.</p>
<p>The government said last year it preferred an offer by Lagardere for the Thomson group over a rival bid by Alcatel Alsthom, but had to call off the sale after the Privatisation Commission objected. It is now selling defence electronics company Thomson-CSF alone.</p>
<p>&quot;The French government -- in indicating the procedure chosen for the privatisation of Thomson-CSF, practically confirmed in its statement all elements of the project which we presented last year and which won us victory over our competitor,&quot; Lagardere said in a statement.</p>
</text>
